{
    "$comment": "Which files each kept document describes [scope-35]. gates/check-drift.mjs --check refuses a commit where a listed source moved and the document did not; after reading (and, if needed, updating) the document, `npm run drift:seen -- <doc>` rerecords its hashes. `hash` is sha256 over the sorted lines `<path>\\0<sha256 of content>\\n` of the matched tracked files, `files` holds those per-file hashes, `doc` the document's own sha256. Generated outputs (dist/, site/, docs/MINIFIED.md) are never sources. Not infallible: touching a document counts as looking at it, and the gate knows files, not meaning.",
    "documents": {
        "README.md": {
            "why": "The front page promises what a consumer installs and imports: the exports and version (package.json), the gate count it states (.claude/hooks/gates.sh), the theme list and hook vocabulary (themes/order.json, themes/hooks.json), the fonts (fonts/families.json), the JavaScript entry points it walks through (index.js, js/auto.js, js/strings.js, js/locale.js, js/lazy-register.js, js/theme-picker.js, js/no-flash.js), the component count (components/*.d.ts: one per component, moves with the API, not with every fix), the Tailwind bridge and the Home Assistant generator. css/themes.css is generated (its generator is named instead) and css/*.css as a whole is left out: the README names files, not rules. Narrowed at scope-78: the .d.ts of each named module instead of its .js, and without package.json and gates/generate-themes.mjs.",
